MID_EV20_026_m01_081: 
MID_EV20_026_m01_082: 
MID_EV20_026_m01_002: Our scouts should have returned by now. Has there\nbeen no word from them?
MID_EV20_026_m01_003: These were no ordinary scouts. They spent months\nin Dagsion as part of Your Majesty's retinue.
MID_EV20_026_m01_004: Knowing that this could be an empty-fort strategy,\nI ordered them to be thorough.
MID_EV20_026_m01_005: I understand your anxiety, but give them time.
MID_EV20_026_m01_006: Well, it's a big city. They're probably just taking their\ntime to make sure they cover it all.
MID_EV20_026_m01_007: It's just like you said, Peter. An empty city just\nisn't right. I can't believe everyone's gone.
MID_EV20_026_m01_008: Yeah. I can't believe it either.
MID_EV20_026_m01_009: About a million people live in Dagsion.
MID_EV20_026_m01_010: They can't all have just vanished. What is going on?
MID_EV20_026_m01_011: I...did hear something about the revival of\nDagda's cauldron.
MID_EV20_026_m01_012: Cai, do you remember the mural we saw in the\ndead city, Ahm Lu?
MID_EV20_026_m01_013: The people of Dagsion... You don't think...
MID_EV20_026_m01_014: There are several variants of the empty-fort\nstrategy, are there not?
MID_EV20_026_m01_015: Indeed. One such variant lures enemies in before\nexterminating them by flame or flood.
MID_EV20_026_m01_016: Others employ the same tactic but rely on a large\nforce for their killing power.
MID_EV20_026_m01_017: A particularly novel version plays on an enemy's\nfear of the strategy, despite a truly empty fort.
MID_EV20_026_m01_018: Queen Theodora! The scouts have returned.
MID_EV20_026_m01_019: Good. I would know the situation inside the city.
MID_EV20_026_m01_020: I can't explain why, but...we didn't encounter a single\nsoul in Dagsion.
MID_EV20_026_m01_021: The city streets should have been packed, but instead\nwe found them empty.
MID_EV20_026_m01_022: And your search was thorough and complete?
MID_EV20_026_m01_023: Of course. We checked everywhere apart from\nDagda the Great's own temple.
MID_EV20_026_m01_024: But there were no signs of life in the residential\nareas, the harbor, or even the sewers.
MID_EV20_026_m01_025: They were clearly living here until recently, but now\nit's as if they all vanished into thin air.
MID_EV20_026_m01_026: Impossible. How could a million citizens disappear\nwithout a trace?
MID_EV20_026_m01_027: There's one more thing. The colosseum has been\ntorn down, and there's a huge hole where it stood.
MID_EV20_026_m01_028: 
MID_EV20_026_m01_029: 
MID_EV20_026_m01_030: 
MID_EV20_026_m01_031: 
MID_EV20_026_m01_032: 
MID_EV20_026_m01_033: No... Even he would not go to such extremes.
MID_EV20_026_m01_034: But if I am wrong...if the million souls in Dagsion\nare gone for the reasons I fear...
MID_EV20_026_m01_035: Then I will hound that self-styled god to the depths\nof the underworld until he is no more!
MID_EV20_026_m01_036: I feel as you do, but anger will not serve us now.
MID_EV20_026_m01_037: If nothing else, we have to confirm our fears by\nspeaking with the emperor ourselves.
MID_EV20_026_m01_038: "All who cross great Dagda regret the grave mistake.
MID_EV20_026_m01_039: "He boils them in his cauldron, and of their\nstew partakes."
MID_EV20_026_m01_040: Where did you hear that unsettling poem,\nMiss Leda?
MID_EV20_026_m01_041: It's a stanza from a book Cohen wrote, passed down\nin House Cohendia.
MID_EV20_026_m01_042: A collection of verses he'd heard other bards sing\nduring his travels.
MID_EV20_026_m01_043: There are whispers about the cauldron having\nbeen restored.
MID_EV20_026_m01_044: Unnerving to think the Divine Emperor means to\nuse that despicable device once more...
MID_EV20_026_m01_045: Heh. So he would sacrifice a million souls to achieve\nhis own aims. Impressive.
MID_EV20_026_m01_046: Impressive, perhaps. Cruel, certainly.
MID_EV20_026_m01_047: I am fascinated. It cost him so many of his citizens.
MID_EV20_026_m01_048: Just what did he get in exchange?
MID_EV20_026_m01_049: The power he wields... It is unimaginable.
MID_EV20_026_m01_050: Perhaps the elation I have been seeking is at hand.
MID_EV20_026_m01_051: 
MID_EV20_026_m01_052: 
MID_EV20_026_m01_053: 
MID_EV20_026_m01_054: 
MID_EV20_026_m01_055: 
MID_EV20_026_m01_056: 
MID_EV20_026_m01_057: 
MID_EV20_026_m01_058: 
MID_EV20_026_m01_059: 
MID_EV20_026_m01_060: 
MID_EV20_026_m01_061: 
MID_EV20_026_m01_062: Before we depart, I should note that Father is likely\nto assume dragon form again for our final battle.
MID_EV20_026_m01_063: That is troubling. It was only through Troy's\nintervention that we drove him off last time.
MID_EV20_026_m01_064: Can such a creature be bested by mere mortals?
MID_EV20_026_m01_065: I think so. No matter how powerful he is, there's a\nflaw we can exploit.
MID_EV20_026_m01_066: A dragon's brow is adorned by something called a\ngodshield, protecting the heart directly behind it.
MID_EV20_026_m01_067: Destroying it is not a simple task, but doing so would\nmake it possible to deliver a fatal wound.
MID_EV20_026_m01_068: If we fight smart, that could be our best hope at\nvictory over Father.
MID_EV20_027_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV20_027_m01_069: 
MID_EV20_027_m01_070: 
MID_EV20_027_m01_071: 
MID_EV20_027_m01_072: 
MID_EV20_027_m01_073: 
MID_EV20_027_m01_074: 
MID_EV20_027_m01_075: 
MID_EV20_027_m01_076: 
MID_EV20_027_m01_077: 
MID_EV20_027_m01_001: Had a hard time with Lind, didn't you, little ones?
MID_EV20_027_m01_002: I beg you to stop this, Divine Emperor.
MID_EV20_027_m01_003: Is that you, Jurah? And Credna too. I didn't think\nyou'd stoop to join their cause.
MID_EV20_027_m01_004: Especially you, Credna. I took you for a coward too\nscared to even look me in the eye.
MID_EV20_027_m01_005: But here you are, standing tall and defying me.\nI can respect the effort.
MID_EV20_027_m01_006: Trust me, Father, I'm scared—so scared, I could\nfall down right here.
MID_EV20_027_m01_007: But I've always had misgivings. I still regret saying\nnothing when you executed Yu Phas.
MID_EV20_027_m01_008: And so I finally found the courage to help these\npeople stop you.
MID_EV20_027_m01_009: Mm. You're a little late for that.
MID_EV20_027_m01_010: There's only one draft left for me to drink.
MID_EV20_027_m01_011: *gulp* *gulp* *gulp* Ahhhh.
MID_EV20_027_m01_012: No... You cannot be drinking what I think you are.
MID_EV20_027_m01_013: But I am. Every citizen of Dagsion was condemned\nto death in my cauldron.
MID_EV20_027_m01_014: One million souls' worth of flamma—all for me.
MID_EV20_027_m01_015: Bastard! What gives you the right?
MID_EV20_027_m01_016: 
MID_EV20_027_m01_017: 
MID_EV20_027_m01_018: 
MID_EV20_027_m01_019: 
MID_EV20_027_m01_020: 
MID_EV20_027_m01_021: 
MID_EV20_027_m01_022: 
MID_EV20_027_m01_023: 
MID_EV20_027_m01_024: 
MID_EV20_027_m01_025: Little one, you may as well be a bird chirping on a\nbranch for all the difference it makes.
MID_EV20_027_m01_026: Bwahahaha!
MID_EV20_027_m01_027: There is my argument. A single swing of my arm was\nalmost enough to overpower you.
MID_EV20_027_m01_028: Well, Raksha? Am I stronger than the progenitor\ngod yet?
MID_EV20_027_m01_029: Indeed, Divine Emperor. Your strength is superior\nnow even to hers.
MID_EV20_027_m01_030: What have you left to fear? You are free to impose\nyour will without mercy.
MID_EV20_027_m01_031: You OK, boss?!
MID_EV20_027_m01_032: I did not want to believe it, but I can no longer deny\nthe truth.
MID_EV20_027_m01_033: Some part of me still respected you for building such\na grand empire.
MID_EV20_027_m01_034: For am I not also royalty charged with seeing my\npeople flourish?
MID_EV20_027_m01_035: The sacrifices at Fezzan... The senseless razing\nof Damascar...
MID_EV20_027_m01_036: I thought there must have been some greater purpose\nto it all. But now I see you clearly.
MID_EV20_027_m01_037: Your people—those placed under your care—never\nmeant anything to you!
MID_EV20_027_m01_038: No true monarch, no matter how corrupt, would\ndebase himself so utterly!
MID_EV20_027_m01_039: Silence, worm! I've had all I can stomach of you.
MID_EV20_027_m01_040: I could say the same, blackguard. The people's lives\nare not your playthings.
MID_EV20_027_m01_041: I vow on my name that you will be a blight upon\nthem no longer!
MID_EV20_027_m01_042: 
MID_EV20_027_m01_043: 
MID_EV20_027_m01_044: Do humans mean anything to you?
MID_EV20_027_m01_045: So many people lived in this city, some good,\nsome bad.
MID_EV20_027_m01_046: Some were in love, some had children.
MID_EV20_027_m01_047: Some were dreamers, living their lives to the fullest.
MID_EV20_027_m01_048: I don't care who the hell you are. I won't stand\nfor this.
MID_EV20_027_m01_049: I will avenge this city!
MID_EV20_027_m01_050: I hope you are prepared, he who is called\nDivine Emperor.
MID_EV20_027_m01_051: Standing before you, I am swept up in anticipation.\nMy heart dances like it did when I was a boy.
MID_EV20_027_m01_052: Show me the power you traded a million lives for!
MID_EV20_027_m01_053: Come! Let us enjoy this, the dance of damnation!
MID_EV20_027_m01_054: I've killed many people...in each of them, I could still\nrecognize at least a shred of humanity.
MID_EV20_027_m01_055: Standing face to face with you, I see none.
MID_EV20_027_m01_056: You're nothing like the others I've killed—and you\ndon't deserve my sympathy.
MID_EV20_027_m01_057: I'm going to slay you, and then I won't have to look\nat your disgusting face ever again.
MID_EV20_027_m01_058: 
MID_EV20_027_m01_059: 
MID_EV20_027_m01_060: 
MID_EV20_027_m01_061: 
MID_EV20_027_m01_062: 
MID_EV20_027_m01_063: 
MID_EV20_027_m01_064: 
MID_EV20_027_m01_065: 
MID_EV20_027_m01_066: 
MID_EV20_027_m01_067: 
MID_EV20_027_m01_068: Bark all you want, little mortal. When the dust\nsettles, you'll know the meaning of absolute power!
MID_EV20_030_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV20_030_m01_001: Long have you waited, Father. And now the moment\nhas arrived at last.
MID_EV20_030_m01_002: We tread a long, long road to reach this moment. So\nmany dupes have I puppeted to their demise.
MID_EV20_030_m01_003: And all of it for this.
MID_EV20_030_m01_004: The time has come for the underworld contained in\nyou to be made incarnate in our world.
MID_EV20_030_m01_005: If only I had been able to recover all your remains...
MID_EV20_030_m01_006: But everything I collected has been gathered here.
MID_EV20_030_m01_007: It should be enough of your body that you can regain\nmost of your former strength.
MID_EV20_030_m01_008: In mere moments, the flamma extracted from a\ncorrupted Founder will rain down upon us.
MID_EV20_030_m01_009: I shall become the mother who ushers in your second\nbirth, Father.
MID_EV20_030_m01_010: Return that I might see you again!
MID_EV20_030_m01_011: Ohhh... Ah...